---
name: get_sys_audio
description: >-
  Use when hearing/capturing live system playback on the owner's computer (Mac,
  Windows, or Linux) or when get_sys_audio is invoked — not for web downloads.
  Never change default audio output without approval that turn.
---
# get_sys_audio (cross-platform)

**FAIL CLOSED:** Capture runs on the parent agent with Shell + machineId on the owner's registered computer. Never dispatch to a box-only executor.

**NEVER change the audio route without explicit user approval in that turn** (default output, aggregates, virtual cables, headphones/speakers/interface flips).

Capture live system playback and listen to a short clip. Do not download audio from websites unless explicitly asked.

## Platform detection
Use the machine they messaged from or named (check ListMachines connected). Detect OS, follow its section; prefer paths that don't change the default output; else explain setup or take an attached clip.

## macOS 13+ — DEFAULT: ScreenCaptureKit (no BlackHole, no route change)
One-time: swiftc (Xcode CLT: xcode-select --install) and ffmpeg (brew install ffmpeg). Save the source below as ~/Documents/handel-capture/tool/sysaudio.swift and compile: cd ~/Documents/handel-capture/tool && swiftc -O sysaudio.swift -o sysaudio. First run: macOS blocks it until the owner enables System Settings → Privacy & Security → Screen & System Audio Recording for the app that runs the agent's commands (error -3801 'user declined TCCs' = permission off). That is a permission grant, not a route change.

Capture: cd ~/Documents/handel-capture && ./tool/sysaudio clip.caf 20; ffmpeg -y -i clip.caf clip.wav; ffmpeg -i clip.wav -af volumedetect -f null - (reject silence, mean about -91 dB); wrap to MP4 with a black video track (ffmpeg -y -f lavfi -i color=c=black:s=320x180:r=5 -i clip.wav -shortest -c:v libx264 -c:a aac clip.mp4); CopyToBox from Documents (not /tmp); watchVideo listen report. The song must be playing during capture.

Source (sysaudio.swift):
```swift
import Foundation
import ScreenCaptureKit
import AVFoundation
import CoreMedia

final class Rec: NSObject, SCStreamOutput, SCStreamDelegate {
    var file: AVAudioFile?
    let url: URL
    init(url: URL) { self.url = url }
    func stream(_ s: SCStream, didOutputSampleBuffer sb: CMSampleBuffer, of type: SCStreamOutputType) {
        guard type == .audio, sb.isValid else { return }
        try? sb.withAudioBufferList { abl, _ in
            guard let desc = sb.formatDescription?.audioStreamBasicDescription else { return }
            var d = desc
            guard let fmt = AVAudioFormat(streamDescription: &d),
                  let buf = AVAudioPCMBuffer(pcmFormat: fmt, bufferListNoCopy: abl.unsafePointer) else { return }
            if file == nil { file = try? AVAudioFile(forWriting: url, settings: fmt.settings) }
            try? file?.write(from: buf)
        }
    }
    func stream(_ s: SCStream, didStopWithError e: Error) { print("stopped: \(e)") }
}
let secs = Double(CommandLine.arguments.count > 2 ? CommandLine.arguments[2] : "15") ?? 15
let out = URL(fileURLWithPath: CommandLine.arguments.count > 1 ? CommandLine.arguments[1] : "out.caf")
let rec = Rec(url: out)
Task {
    do {
        let c = try await SCShareableContent.current
        guard let disp = c.displays.first else { print("no display"); exit(2) }
        let f = SCContentFilter(display: disp, excludingWindows: [])
        let cfg = SCStreamConfiguration()
        cfg.capturesAudio = true
        cfg.excludesCurrentProcessAudio = true
        cfg.sampleRate = 48000; cfg.channelCount = 2
        cfg.width = 2; cfg.height = 2
        let s = SCStream(filter: f, configuration: cfg, delegate: rec)
        try s.addStreamOutput(rec, type: .audio, sampleHandlerQueue: DispatchQueue(label: "a"))
        try await s.startCapture()
        try await Task.sleep(nanoseconds: UInt64(secs * 1e9))
        try await s.stopCapture()
        print("done \(out.path)")
        exit(0)
    } catch { print("ERR: \(error)"); exit(1) }
}
RunLoop.main.run()
```

Fallback (older macOS or permission refused): BlackHole 2ch plus a Multi-Output (real output + BlackHole) already in the listening path; record BlackHole with ffmpeg avfoundation. Never flip the default without approval that turn; restore the exact prior device.

## Windows
Prefer WASAPI loopback: Python 3 + pip install soundcard numpy; record 6–15s from soundcard.get_microphone(id=default_speaker.name, include_loopback=True) to WAV in Documents; don't change the default playback device. Alternate: VB-CABLE + ffmpeg dshow capture of CABLE Output (arrangement only with approval); Stereo Mix if already enabled.

## Linux
PulseAudio/PipeWire monitor, no default-sink change: pactl list short sources → *.monitor; ffmpeg -f pulse -i <monitor> -t 15 ~/Music/clip.wav; volumedetect; copy; MP4 wrap; listen.

## Shared rules
No unapproved route changes; restore after any approved change; no website scraping; clips 15–30s; never /tmp alone for CopyToBox; if capture can't work after an honest attempt, one blocker + attached-clip fallback.

## Done
Capture worked/failed, default output confirmed unchanged, short listening summary — or one blocker, or proceed with an attached clip.
